 "notes": "GEO600 scalar-field DM search. Curve traced from the vector paths of the green 'This work' boundary in Fig. 2 (Basic Scalar scenario, file figures/BasicScalar_PaperR2.0_NATURE_Lambda_Excl._08-26-2021_1121.pdf), calibrated with the MATLAB gridlines (x: 1e-20..1e-5 eV, y: 1e-30..1e-10 GeV^-1); extracted curve spans 2.07e-13 eV (=50 Hz) to 2.4e-11 eV (~5.8 kHz), matching the stated analysis band. Paper reports 95% CL upper limits on 1/Lambda_gamma (and identically on 1/Lambda_e, since the signal in Eq. 6 is proportional to 1/Lambda_gamma + 1/Lambda_e and each coupling is bounded with the other set to zero). Converted to Damour-Donoghue d_e via delta_alpha/alpha = phi/Lambda_gamma = d_e*kappa*phi, i.e. d_e = (1/Lambda_gamma) * M_Pl/sqrt(4pi) with M_Pl = 1.22e19 GeV (factor 3.4416e18 GeV). The identical curve applies to d_me (ScalarElectron). Basic Scalar scenario chosen as the main result; Dilaton/Modulus and Relaxion Halo scenarios in Fig. 3 are model variants. Assumed local DM density 0.4 GeV/cm^3; limit minimum d_e ~ 0.16 at m ~ 1e-12 eV.",
